# Component Standards

## Architecture

```text
app/                    # routes only: metadata + compose sections
components/
  layout/               # Header, Footer, MobileMenu, Marquee, CookieBanner
  ui/                   # Button, Container, SectionHeader, Link
  sections/             # PageHero, CtaBand, FAQ, feature blocks
  mega-menu/            # Why / Platform / Solutions / Industries / Pricing / Company
```

## Rules

1. **Pages are thin.** A route file exports `metadata` and renders imported section components only.
2. **One component = one job.** No 500-line page components with header+hero+footer inlined.
3. **Shared chrome once.** Header, Footer, CTA band, Cookie banner live in root/marketing layout — not duplicated per page.
4. **Designs → components.** When porting HTML, extract repeating blocks first; leaf content second.
5. **Client only when needed.** Prefer Server Components; add `"use client"` for menus, tabs, FAQ accordion, IntersectionObserver reveals.
6. **Props over copy-paste.** Eyebrow/title/body/cta via props on `SectionHeader`, `PageHero`, `CtaBand`.
7. **No cards in heroes.** Match Designs; sitewide cards use `rounded-[4px]` panels only where Designs do.
8. **Colocate** page-specific sections under `components/sections/<page>/` if not reused.

## Page shape

```tsx
// app/pricing/page.tsx
export const metadata = { … };

export default function PricingPage() {
  return (
    <>
      <PageHero … />
      <PricingTiers … />
      <PricingFaqTeaser … />
    </>
  );
}
```

## Shared components to build first

`Container`, `Button`, `SiteHeader`, `MobileMenu`, `MegaMenu`, `SiteFooter`, `CtaBand`, `PageHero`, `SectionHeader`, `CookieBanner`, `MarqueeTopBar`
